{0 IMITATOR API reference}

This is the {e internal} API reference for IMITATOR, generated from the
documentation comments in the source code with {{:https://ocaml.github.io/odoc/}odoc}.

It is aimed at {b contributors and developers} working on IMITATOR itself.
End users should instead read the user guide (see [doc/user-guide]), and
contributors may also want the developer manual (see [doc/developer-manual]).

{1 Building this reference}

From the repository root:

{[
  opam install odoc
  doc/scripts/build-api-reference.sh
]}

The HTML is generated under [_build/default/_doc/_html/] and bundled under
[doc/api/html/]; open [doc/api/html/index.html] to browse the custom landing
page and jump into the odoc-generated package reference.

{2 Why [@doc-private]?}

IMITATOR is built as a set of {e private} libraries (they have no
[public_name]), so the public [@doc] alias would document almost nothing.
The [@doc-private] alias documents the internal libraries and their modules.

{1 Libraries}

The code is organised into the following libraries, each documented through
its top-level wrapped module:

- {{:../utils@75a864dae907/Utils/index.html}utils} — general-purpose helpers
- {{:../data_structures@75a864dae907/Data_structures/index.html}data_structures} — reusable data structures and caches
- {{:../parsing@75a864dae907/Parsing/index.html}parsing} — model and property parsers
- {{:../entities@75a864dae907/Entities/index.html}entities} — core data types
- {{:../lib@75a864dae907/Lib/index.html}lib} — shared model-checking infrastructure
- {{:../algorithms@75a864dae907/Algorithms/index.html}algorithms} — the synthesis and verification algorithms
- {{:../exporter@75a864dae907/Exporter/index.html}exporter} — output and export back-ends
